# EDA Summary Report

## Overview

The Telco Customer Churn dataset was explored to understand customer characteristics and factors related to churn.

## Key Observations

* The dataset contained no missing values.
* No duplicate records were found.
* Categorical features were encoded for model training.
* Numerical features showed different value ranges, so feature scaling was applied.
* Customer-related attributes such as contract type, tenure, monthly charges, and internet services showed noticeable relationships with churn.

## Conclusion

The dataset was clean and suitable for machine learning. After preprocessing and feature engineering, multiple classification models were trained and compared to identify the best-performing model for customer churn prediction.
